NUM-53: give control rules the rule step, not the routing step, when RULE_STEP > 0

With RULE_STEP > 0 the rules are evaluated once per rule step, but
SWMMEngine::stepRouting() passed the current routing step as the
evaluation's time step. That step is the width of the "=" window for
SIMULATION TIME / CLOCKTIME / TIMEOPEN / TIMECLOSED premises, which became
narrower than the spacing of the evaluations (a premise such as
"CLOCKTIME = 01:03:00" never held), and the dt of a PID action, whose
integral and derivative terms were scaled by the routing step although the
controller acts once per rule step. Pass the rule step instead.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-53_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..d4a7040 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -4693,7 +4693,10 @@ void SWMMEngine::stepRouting(double dt_routing) noexcept {
     const bool rule_time_reached =
         ctx_.options.rule_step <= 0.0 ||
         std::fabs(ctx_.elapsed_ms - new_rule_time_ms_) < 1.0;
-    controls_.evaluate(ctx_, routing_date, dt_routing, rule_time_reached);
+    // An evaluation covers one rule step when RULE_STEP > 0.
+    controls_.evaluate(ctx_, routing_date,
+                       ctx_.options.rule_step > 0.0 ? ctx_.options.rule_step : dt_routing,
+                       rule_time_reached);
     // Apply setting transitions: move setting toward target_setting
     for (int j = 0; j < ctx_.n_links(); ++j) {
         auto uj = static_cast<std::size_t>(j);
